      "recommended_risk": "low",
      "title": "Anthropic API key sent directly from the browser to the provider endpoint",
      "technical_explanation": "Most providers route requests through the SillyTavern backend proxy endpoint using host request headers, which keeps credentials and CORS handling server-side. The Anthropic branch instead performs a direct browser fetch to the Anthropic messages endpoint with the user-supplied key in a request header. The destination is the legitimate, hard-coded provider endpoint selected by the user, and the key travels only to that provider, so this is an ordinary direct-to-provider pattern rather than exfiltration. It does differ from the proxy pattern used for other providers and relies on the provider's CORS support.",
      "layman_explanation": "For one provider, the extension contacts the AI service directly from the browser instead of going through SillyTavern's own server. The key still only goes to the legitimate service it belongs to, so nothing is leaked, but the approach is inconsistent with how other providers are handled.",
      "developer_action": "Consider routing the Anthropic call through the same SillyTavern backend proxy path used for the other providers for consistency and to avoid browser-side credential handling.",
      "locations": [
        {
          "path": "api-providers.js",
          "line_start": 65,
          "line_end": 65
        }
      ]
    }
